<br/><br/><br/><br/>
Milestones in the history of TimerMod<br/><br/>

<style type="text/css">
table.history td
{
	border-top: 1px solid #CCCC99;
	vertical-align: top;
}
table.history td.date
{
	text-align: right;
	font-weight: normal;
	font-size: 10px;
}
</style>

<table class="history" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="8">
<tr><td class="date">August&nbsp;11<br/>2002</td><td><div style="float: right; text-align: center; font-size: 10px; margin-left: 12px; margin-bottom: 8px; margin-bottom: 8px"><a href="image/history/dialexample.jpg" target="_blank"><img src="image/history/dialexample-thumbnail.jpg" border="0" width="160" height="120"><br/>(click to enlarge)</a></div><img src="image/history/dial-prototype.jpg" width="52" height="52" style="float: left; margin-right: 12px; margin-bottom: 8px">The original tick timer was introduced. This timer consisted of a one-minute dial divided into 10 six-second ticks. The download package included a custom timer XML file and TGA image, requiring users to incorporate the timer element into one of their own windows. The provided example, shown on the right, embeds the tick dial in the target window.</td></tr>
<tr><td class="date">August&nbsp;13<br/>2002</td><td><img src="image/history/dialdigital-1.jpg" width="109" height="158" style="float: left; margin-right: 12px; margin-bottom: 8px">The timer was changed so that it occupied its own window, making it easier for users to add the timer to their UI. 10 tabs were added to the top of the tick dial which allowed users to "mark" one of the ticks when timing. A one-hour digital timer was also added at the bottom of the window. The timer and website were given the name <b>Mez/Spawn Timer</b>.</td></tr>
<tr><td class="date">August&nbsp;15<br/>2002</td><td>New timer configurations were made available for download, allowing users to choose from a few different windows for the timer. A combination pet/timer window was also made available (some timer later, a few additional "combo" mods were added, including hotkeys/timer and actions/timer).</td></tr>
<tr><td class="date">August&nbsp;16<br/>2002</td><td>The timer XML was restructured so that it was self-contained and had no dependencies. This allowed the timer to remain unaffected by patch changes in other parts of the UI. Installation was also much easier because manual modifications were no longer necessary.</td></tr>
<tr><td class="date">August&nbsp;19<br/>2002</td><td>The web-based XML generator was introduced in order to satisfy numerous requests for custom timer configurations. Users could choose whether they want the tick dial (with or without markers), the digital timer, or both. Other options include the window used as well as various title bar styles. For users who wish to embed other elements into the timer window, advanced options such as offset, window size, title, transparency, and border were also made available.<br/><br/>When the user finished configuring the timer, the server dynamically generated a custom XML file for download. The user would place this file in the mod folder along with the timer graphics file (downloaded separately). For the convenience of users who did not require special customizations, the most popular configurations were pre-generated and made into ready-to-download packages.</td></tr>
<tr><td class="date">September&nbsp;2<br/>2002</td><td><img src="image/history/dialdigital-2.jpg" width="96" height="138" style="float: left; margin-right: 12px; margin-bottom: 8px">A more compact version of the dial/digital timer was released. New options were added for the digital timer so that it has a customizable duration (up to 10 hours) and can be configured to count either up or down.</td></tr>
<tr><td class="date">September&nbsp;24<br/>2002</td><td><img src="image/history/slider-prototype.jpg" width="155" height="67" style="float: left; margin-right: 12px; margin-bottom: 8px">A prototype of the slider timer was made available for testing and feedback. This new type of timer used a looping bar animation matching the duration of the event to be timed (in this example, 6 minutes for mend). To begin timing, the user would place the slider at the current position of the bar. The bar would continue on and reach the slider's position again when one full duration of the timer has elapsed.<br/><br/>This particular prototype used a real slider element, which exhibited granularity problems because it was not linked to an actual range of values by the game client. In the released version of the slider timer, this problem was solved by using a horizontal scrollbar to represent the slider.</td></tr>
<tr><td class="date">September&nbsp;28<br/>2002</td><td><img src="image/history/slider.jpg" width="204" height="124" style="float: left; margin-right: 12px; margin-bottom: 8px">The slider timer was released as an additional type of timer available from the site. Using the custom XML generator, the user could configure up to eight slider timers, each with a custom name, color, and duration. The timer and website's name was changed to <b>UI Timer</b>.</td></tr>
<tr><td class="date">September&nbsp;29<br/>2002</td><td><img src="image/history/dialdigital-3.jpg" width="96" height="114" style="float: left; margin-right: 12px; margin-bottom: 8px">The tab-based markers on the dial timer were replaced with button-based markers. This not only made the dial easier to use but also saved space as well, since the row of tabs was no longer necessary.</td></tr>
<tr><td class="date">October&nbsp;1<br/>2002</td><td>The timer XML generator was modified to output window-specific identifiers for each element. This allowed multiple timer windows to be used together without conflict.</td></tr>
<tr><td class="date">October&nbsp;2<br/>2002</td><td>A new option was added allowing the slider timers to be arranged in a column or row. Previously, they could only be arranged in a column.</td></tr>
<tr><td class="date">October&nbsp;20<br/>2002</td><td><img src="image/history/slider-compact.jpg" width="146" height="124" style="float: left; margin-right: 12px; margin-bottom: 8px">A compact version of the slider timer was released. The maximum number of timers was increased to 12, and new layout options were added to allow for multiple columns/rows of timers. A new section was added to the website featuring user-submitted skins for the slider timer.</td></tr>
<tr><td class="date">October&nbsp;29<br/>2002</td><td>The slider timer duration could now be specified in one-second increments (instead of six-second increments) for more precision.</td></tr>
<tr><td class="date">May&nbsp;8<br/>2003</td><td>The file download mechanism was enhanced. Previously, the dynamically-generated XML was output to the user directly, which required the user to save it as a file using the proper name as well as download the graphics file separately. With the new changes, the XML file is output to a temporary file on the server, then zipped up along with the TGA image file in a single downloadable package. This made the installation process much easier, because users could now simply unzip the files into their mod folder.</td></tr>
<tr><td class="date">June&nbsp;2<br/>2004</td><td><img src="image/screenshot/tooltip.jpg" width="259" height="51" style="float: left; margin-right: 12px; margin-bottom: 8px">The new timer website was launched and a new type of timer was introduced. This timer uses a bar animation and works similarly to the slider timer, but instead of a slider, it uses a button-based marker which can be set easily and quickly with a single click.<br/><br/>Many more customization options were added, including icons, configurable length, horizontal/vertical timers, split markers, and multiple tabbed pages of timers. Support was added for many additional windows and duration calculators were made available for users to facilitate timer configuration. The timer and website's name was changed to <b>TimerMod</b>.</td></tr>
</table>



